  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by hand, then ran the function, which printed the same number.\n\nThe function uses only `pricing` and `discounts`:\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: 600 \u2212 600 \u00d7 20 // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result. `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` only holds an empty bundle config and has no effect either.\n\nANSWER: 480",
